# RFQ Auto-Quoter & OMS — Functional Spec (v2, Proposed)

> **Scope of this document.** This is a *capability* specification: what the system must **do**, the data it must hold, and the surfaces it must expose. It deliberately contains **no modelling decisions** — estimator choices, signal construction, and pricing math live in a separate quant spec (see §8, Out of Scope).

---

## 1. Vision & Target Workflow

The engine **quotes by default**; the trader **supervises, overrides, and tunes guards** rather than clicking per inquiry.

Perfect-state loop:

1. RFQs flow into the UI in real time across the full whitelisted universe.
2. The pricing engine generates levels for every in-universe RFQ it has enough information to price.
3. The trader confirms levels and guards once, then turns on auto-quote with **one click**.
4. The responder decides which RFQs to answer, sends levels, and **re-quotes without trader intervention**.
5. The trader monitors, intervenes on exceptions, diagnoses misses, and improves the engine.

The same one-stop interface must also carry **make + take + sweeps** (send RFQs, take liquidity, run other protocols) — not just passive response.

---

## 2. System Components

| Component | Role |
|---|---|
| **RFQ Responder / Auto-Quoter** | Decides whether to answer each live RFQ; sends and updates levels under cadence rules. |
| **Pricing Engine** | Produces a level, an edge, a fill-likelihood, and a **confidence** per inquiry. |
| **Risk-Gate Layer** | Hard gate, *separate from pricing*. Single-name guards **plus** aggregate in-flight budget **plus** hedge-capacity checks. |
| **Signals / Market-Data Layer** | Feeds the engine: TRACE prints, dealer runs/axes, ECN stack, BBG runs, issuer equity, ETF flow → one **consolidated market-pressure signal**. |
| **Hedging Interface** | Exposes current hedge capacity and cost (CDX / ETF / duration) to the engine. |
| **Trader Dashboard** | Always-on surface: blotter, per-inquiry detail, overrides, bias/protection toggles, lineage. |
| **OMS** | **Event-sourced system of record.** The spine both responder and dashboard read from; replayable. |

