## 3. Original Capabilities (baseline — carried forward)

These exist in the current design and **must be preserved**.

**Response / auto-quoter**
- Auto-respond toggle across the desired universe (whole whitelist → autoquote, no click-per-inquiry).
- Respond/pull quotes from a single dash-style surface carrying all relevant bond information.
- All accessible RFQs flow through; **no per-bond filtering** unless out-of-universe / not approved.
- **Centralized do-not-quote rule set**, evaluated as a final step (stock move, intraday move, earnings flag, missing ECN side, low amount outstanding, liquidity threshold, size threshold, position-post-trade threshold, lowest-alpha quintile, settlement edge cases, etc.).
- **Explainability**: ability to state plainly *why* an RFQ did not get auto-quoted.
- **Manual level override** per inquiry.
- **Toggleable bias**: uniform wider ↔ more aggressive (price up/down on bid, offer side; at universe, grid, and ISIN level).
- **Toggleable protections**: don't quote through ECN, don't quote through dealer, off-market TRACE-print protection (bid/offer amounts in cents or spread).
- **1-click off per bond** on bid / offer / both — persist permanent or reset daily.
- **In-flight controls**: time remaining to respond, killswitch to pull responded levels, live level update.
- **Cadence**: *ASAP* (respond instantly, re-quote on ≥ 1c move) and *Binned* (price as close to due time as possible, pull if FV moves beyond threshold).

**Trade-flow surface**
- Staged flow: Universe Live → Engine Prices → Trader Sanity Check → Auto-Respond.
- Trader dashboard contents: live RFQ blotter with status, per-inquiry inputs, manual override / pull, do-not-quote toggles, bias control, protections, **RFQ-ID → full input lineage**.

**OMS / diagnostics**
- Live RFQs blotter (valid-until, time, feedcode, ISIN/CUSIP/ticker, position, state, workflow, side, size, price type, traded status, universe count).
- Per-CUSIP/ISIN **drill-down**: TRACE prints, ECN stack, dealer quotes, BBG dealer runs.
- Searching a CUSIP surfaces all historical inquiry/trades and reference-price history.
- **API next step (in parallel)**: send RFQs and take liquidity via API from the same surface — set size/direction, pick venue/protocol, receive quotes in-UI, compare vs mid, trade/pass/counter.

